[s0l0!-header][h1]Static [/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The same concept applies to [b]static [/b]methods.[code format="java" ]public class Vehicle {
  public [b]static [/b]void horn() {
    System.out.println("Beep");
  }
}[/code]
Now, the [b]horn [/b]method can be called without creating an object:[code format="java" codeId="770"]public class MyClass {
  public static void main(String[ ] args) {
    Vehicle.horn();
  }
}[/code]
Another example of static methods are those of the [b]Math [/b]class, which is why you can call them without creating a [b]Math [/b]object.
[note]Also, the [b]main[/b] method must always be [b]static[/b].[/note]

